  "discussion": "For north facing shores, small north-northwest swell will fade through the day and tiny surf is anticipated on Friday. Another small north-northwest swell is forecast to arrive and build on Saturday, peaking Saturday night into Sunday, with a larger (advisory level) and longer lived northwest swell expected next Tuesday. A potential XL northwest swell is then possible by the middle of next week as models indicate a strong storm force low pressure system developing far north of the islands next week. However, model discrepancies over the strength and position of the fetch are notable at this time, so the size of the swell is still uncertain. And it looks more likely that any large swell will be accompanied by strong NW or N winds. Rough surf along east-facing shores will hold near seasonal averages today, then increase slightly for Friday and Saturday as trade winds strengthen. A small, long-period swell looks to bring a bump to south shore surf on Friday, and could keep south shore surf slightly elevated through the weekend.",
